ther words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(1,3).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(2,3).$\n\n- The second set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (the corresponding inequality is strict).\n\n- The third set is *closed* since it contains all its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479881 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186479794 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479881 #edb/ref 1069 "q-71811" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479881 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479881 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following sets are neither open nor closed?\n\nI. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le {y}^{2}\\le 4\\}$\n\nII. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<9,\\,0\\le x\\le 3\\}$\n\nIII. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0\\le y<\\sqrt{x},\\,1\\le x\\le 4\\}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479881 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "aa86399c-45ea-5f74-a86a-9df5e96aefc4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479881 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *closed* since it contains all its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\n- The second set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(0,0).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(3,0).$\n\n- The third set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(1,0).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(4,2).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481577 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186481678 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481577 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186481683 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481577 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186481736 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481577 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186481741 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481577 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186481752 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481577 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481577 #edb/ref 1045 "Open and Closed Sets" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481577 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186481741 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481577 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046658 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481577 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048439 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481577 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "cb03d97f-18ef-5754-8c10-bd8c69d187ca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481678 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "103728c3-da2e-5746-827f-d6cd0408ce21" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481678 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186278581 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481683 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186481678 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481683 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1d9ba6fc-d1ed-5998-a6a1-15240e008963" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481683 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186278579 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481736 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186481683 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481736 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d4a32acc-c162-55a3-84e9-b880